BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Northern District Book Club—Afternoons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T150000
UID:6a5f86b17b79214226aa13ae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a friendly\, spirited discussion of a different bo
 ok on the second Wednesday of each month. We read an eclectic mix of mostl
 y contemporary fiction.\nThere is also an evening session to discuss the s
 ame book on the third Wednesday of each month at 7:00 p.m.  You are welc
 ome at either or both!\nNote:\nno August meeting\nSeptember 9\, 2026:\nOrb
 ital\nby Samantha Harvey\nOctober 14\, 2026:\nMaybe You Should Talk to Som
 eone\nby Lori Gottlieb\nNovember 11\, 2026:\nStone Yard Devotional\nby Cha
 rlotte Wood\nDecember 9\, 2026:\nPerfection\nby Vincenzo Latronico
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5f86b17b79214226aa13ae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
