BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grown-ups Reading Children's Literature Book Club: Because of Winn
 -Dixie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T160000
UID:69ff9e4543b41b3d00655b37@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the monthly meeting of Osborne Collection Grown-u
 ps Reading Children's Literature Book Club. It is  for adult readers who 
 enjoy children's books. Revisit favourite stories of your childhood or rea
 d more or less known notable books for young readers for the first time.\n
 We meet once a month on the first or second Saturday (2.30-4PM).\nSeptembe
 r 12: Island of the Blue Dolphins by Scott O’Dell\nOctober 3: A Series o
 f Unfortunate Events: The Bad Beginning by Lemony Snicket\nNovember 14: Bo
 rrowers by Mary Norton\nDecember 5: The BFG by Roald Dahl\nJanuary 9 (2027
 ): Number the Stars by Lois Lowry\nBecause of Winn-Dixie\nBecause of Winn-
 Dixie
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Osborne Collection is located on the 4th floor
  of Lillian H. Smith library.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ff9e4543b41b3d00655b37
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ashdale Writers Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T113000
UID:6a3bdcab86636e3d00503daf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're just setting pen to paper\, or you're a seasone
 d writer\, join us at our bi-weekly Writers Group for inspiration and enco
 uragement in a supportive\, positive environment. We'll warm up with a sho
 rt writing prompt and then you'll have the opportunity to share a portion 
 of your work for feedback from the group.\nThis is a drop-in group.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3bdcab86636e3d00503daf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T150000
UID:69e8e460cdd2f7e31fe2e4a6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. It involves peer-led group activities including 
 crafts\, games\, walking\, yoga and more. Meet new folks\, build connectio
 ns\, and tell us about programs and services you would like to see in the 
 neighbourhood!\nDrop in\, no registration is required.\nThis program is in
  collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:St. Lawrence\, East side of branch\, by tables
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8e460cdd2f7e31fe2e4a6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The SciFi and Fantasy Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T160000
UID:6a3fcce748c98c3600a2bd0f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the book club hosted by The Merril Collection of S
 cience Fiction\, Speculation & Fantasy. Each month we will read a book fro
 m a different sub-genre such as space opera\, high fantasy\, cyberpunk and
  more.\nOur October title is\nThe Amulet of Samarkand\nby Jonathan Stroud.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Collection Reading Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3fcce748c98c3600a2bd0f
