DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nThu
 rsday\, July 23\, 10:00am-12:00pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\
 ,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, July 30-September 17\, 10:00am-1:00pm\n. Regi
 stration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be p
 rovided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingre
 dient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collabo
 ration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis C
 entre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information c
 ollected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca85f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
