DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T153000
UID:6a5d1edbdaaaf4f51a2045d7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to be better prepared to manage future issues. Retir
 ed lawyer\, Sheldon Parker\, offers general information for older adults o
 n three key topics that may likely affect them in the future: Powers of At
 torney\, Will and Codicils\, and Real Estate Ownership Issues.\nA graduate
  of Osgoode Hall Law School\, Sheldon Parker was a founding partner of Par
 ker & Zener LLP\, a law firm specializing in Real Estate\, Commercial\, Ta
 x and Estate work. Retired from active practice in early 2016\, Sheldon no
 w lectures on politics\, fraud\, elder abuse and Estate planning throughou
 t the GTA.\nRegistration is encouraged.\nDrop-ins are welcome until capaci
 ty is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, ground floor
