UID:6a6e59f124cc9f017dda3d96@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of August\, the works of artist Farzana I
 sland are on display at Albion Branch.\nFarzana Islam is a Bangladeshi Ca
 nadian artist and illustrator based in Toronto. She tells stories that don
 ’t always get the spotlight\, aiming to leave a\nfeeling that stays with
  people. From making webcomics as a teen and tattoo apprenticeships to stu
 dying illustration at Sheridan College\, she now\nworks across illustratio
 n\, animation\, and 3D\, bringing untold perspectives to life in human\, m
 eaningful ways.\n"Farzana’s work is rooted in her experience of entering
  the Canadian school system as an immigrant child\, carrying languages and
  stories that didn’t always fit. Shaped by Scarborough’s vibrant dive
 rsity\, her art brings to light how young people carve out belonging withi
 n educational and cultural landscapes. Through her work with youth and he
 r lens as a queer Muslim artist\, she explores identity\, literacy\, and a
 mplifies voices often overlooked but quietly shared across communities."\n
 The exhibit can be viewed during Albion branch's open hours. Please check 
 the\nAlbion branch\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto 
 credit: Farzana Islam\,\nThinking Back\, Watercolour and Coloured Pencil\,
  61 * 91.
LOCATION:Albion
