BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marketing on a Budget
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T200000
UID:6a5668d582c03c5c17d7e6b3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You don't need money to get seen - you need a strategy. In thi
 s session we will cover organic social media\, word of mouth\, community 
 partnerships\, and how to show up consistently without burning out.\nPleas
 e note:  Registered participant spaces will be held for 15 minutes after w
 hich drop-ins will be allowed.\nMeet the Resident:\nVivian Kaye is a seria
 l entrepreneur and business mentor who bootstrapped KinkyCurlyYaki to seve
 n figures without outside funding. Over 15 years\, she has mentored 300+ e
 ntrepreneurs\, recently facilitating workshops for FoundHers Innovation La
 bs and Humber College's Entrepreneurship Program.\nFeatured in The New Yor
 k Times\, Toronto Star\, and on CityTV's Cityline\, Vivian has partnered w
 ith brands including Shopify\, Amazon\, and American Express Canada. Her d
 irect\, practical approach helps early-stage Black entrepreneurs navigate 
 the realities of building sustainable businesses without traditional suppo
 rt systems.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Meeting Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5668d582c03c5c17d7e6b3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T193000
UID:6a6a661db57350d760b31f41@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet online every Thursday evening\,\nSeptember 24 - De
 cember 10\, 6-7:30 PM\n(12 sessions).\nParticipants are expected to commit
  to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekly basis.\nLea
 rners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digital badge\ndown
 load a certificate of completion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f41
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260904T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260904T160000
UID:6a061f5ac6a1dc3d00d3c003@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nFri
 day\, August 14 1:00-4:00 pm.\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\no
 nce a week for 8 weeks\, August 21 to October 9\n. Registration closes aft
 er week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks an
 d refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be
  available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerste
 in Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely res
 ponsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected through th
 e program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Room B1\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a061f5ac6a1dc3d00d3c003
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
