BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Business Inc. Women Entrepreneurs Series - Information Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T120000
UID:6a62458ac7e02e3d006b233c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our Fall 2026 Business Inc. Women Entrepreneurs Informati
 on Session to learn about this 4-week program supporting Toronto entrepren
 eurs to launch and grow.\nDo you have a small business idea and want tailo
 red feedback and support to take it to the next level? Join the Business I
 nc. program to connect with experienced mentors and other entrepreneurs th
 at will help you grow.\nDuring four weekly sessions\, women entrepreneurs 
 will learn business fundamentals\, get clarity on the viability of their b
 usiness ideas\, get feedback and reviews from professional business adviso
 rs\, discuss with and learn from their peers\, and build a foundation for 
 success.\nThe program runs weekly at the S. Walter Stewart Branch on Satur
 days from November 14 - December 5\, from 10am-4pm.\nJoin us at our Inform
 ation Session to learn more about this program\, meet the instructor\, and
  ask any questions you may have about your application.\nLearn about\nBusi
 ness Inc.\n\, a four-week business program offered in partnership with the
  Toronto Business Development Centre.\nWe encourage new or aspiring women 
 entrepreneurs to register\, including those who are cis\, trans and gender
  diverse. Space is limited and registration is required. To register\, cl
 ick\nhere\n.\nThis program is generously supported by Economic Development
  & Culture\, Meridian\, and Toronto Public Library Foundation.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a62458ac7e02e3d006b233c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
