DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T200000
UID:6a5974e0f213992f00c4e0d2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC) workshops are unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect. (wcc-cec.org)\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. 
 Materials are provided.\nWorkshops are not sequential\; every workshop is 
 unique - join any session and let's write together!\nSpace is limited\n. R
 egister online\, in-branch or by calling 416-393-7680.\nThere is one sessi
 on each Tuesday in August. Please register for each session.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room (downstairs)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5974e0f213992f00c4e0d2
