BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Cityscape by Vytik Art Collective
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260830T235959
UID:6a6215c688e9bf280032c552@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of August\, the works of Vytik Art Collec
 tive are on display at Northern District Library.\nVytik Art Collective i
 s a group of emerging visual artists and curators exploring contemporary a
 rt in Toronto. Founded in 2023\, it began as a platform for Ukrainian newc
 omer artists to connect\, collaborate\, and become part of Canada's art co
 mmunity. In just two years\, Vytik has grown into a diverse collective of 
 artists from different cultural and professional backgrounds\, creating ne
 w ways to make and experience art.\n"Intersections" Film & Digital Photogr
 aphy Exhibition brings together 20 emerging and established photographers 
 who express their unique perspectives on urban landscapes through architec
 ture\, streets\, lines\, movement\, and everyday moments of city life:\nAl
 exey Makhinko\, Anastasia Skrypnyk\, Ava Tsarynnyk\, Evan Rajkovic\, Gabri
 el Waddington\, Hadi Amtaeleq\, Jason Hong\, Joshua Kennington\, Kyle Alia
 ly\, Mariia Charuta\, Mark Krzepis\, Marta Kolotylo\, Nicola Jekubik\, Ped
 ro Anao\, Sayani Sarkar\, Sergio Londono Vargas\, Subham Rai\, T.H. Ponder
 s\, Vaishnavi Sambhus\, Yana Tkachenko\n"By successfully curating and mana
 ging two large museum exhibitions featuring over 30 artists\, a solo show 
 of one of our emerging artists\, a group exhibition at an artist-run centr
 e\, Toronto’s largest open call based analog photography show\, and by o
 rganizing more than 10 public workshops\, curatorial tours\, and art event
 s\, Vytik has demonstrated its commitment to accessibility\, experimentati
 on\, and community building. Vytik is rapidly evolving and actively seekin
 g new collaborative opportunities."\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Ex
 hibit\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to
  exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to re
 flect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\n
 The exhibit can be viewed during\nNorthern District\nLibrary open hours.\n
 image credit: Hadi Amtaeleq
LOCATION:Northern District\, 2nd floor Skylight Gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6215c688e9bf280032c552
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
