BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T200000
UID:6a51496188e9bf28002ff5e6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nFri
 day\, October 2\, 5pm-7pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\nonce a 
 week for 8 weeks\, October 9 - November 27\n. Registration closes after we
 ek 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and ref
 reshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be ava
 ilable at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Cr
 isis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsi
 ble for the protection of \npersonal information collected through the pro
 gram registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 200
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a51496188e9bf28002ff5e6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Farzana Islam
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T235959
UID:6a6e59f124cc9f017dda3d8b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of August\, the works of artist Farzana I
 sland are on display at Albion Branch.\nFarzana Islam is a Bangladeshi Ca
 nadian artist and illustrator based in Toronto. She tells stories that don
 ’t always get the spotlight\, aiming to leave a\nfeeling that stays with
  people. From making webcomics as a teen and tattoo apprenticeships to stu
 dying illustration at Sheridan College\, she now\nworks across illustratio
 n\, animation\, and 3D\, bringing untold perspectives to life in human\, m
 eaningful ways.\n"Farzana’s work is rooted in her experience of entering
  the Canadian school system as an immigrant child\, carrying languages and
  stories that didn’t always fit. Shaped by Scarborough’s vibrant dive
 rsity\, her art brings to light how young people carve out belonging withi
 n educational and cultural landscapes. Through her work with youth and he
 r lens as a queer Muslim artist\, she explores identity\, literacy\, and a
 mplifies voices often overlooked but quietly shared across communities."\n
 The exhibit can be viewed during Albion branch's open hours. Please check 
 the\nAlbion branch\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto 
 credit: Farzana Islam\,\nThinking Back\, Watercolour and Coloured Pencil\,
  61 * 91.
LOCATION:Albion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6e59f124cc9f017dda3d8b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
