BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Surviving Dementia Care: The Realities of Family Caregiving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T193000
UID:6a7224bbb46787079ead9120@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This talk is aimed at caregivers of people with dementia. It a
 ddresses the specific experiences of people who are caring for a loved on
 e\, including the various points of stress\, the points of joy\, and ways
  in which caregivers learn to survive the experience.\nLearn about underst
 anding the diagnosis\, communicating with the loved one\, managing guilt 
 and grief\, choosing an assisted living facility\, using music and the ar
 ts as a means of connection and how the loving bond within the family can 
 be maintained for as long as possible.\nPresented by D. Grant Campbell\, a
 uthor of\nSurviving Dementia Care\n(University of Toronto Press\, 2026).\n
 D. Grant Campbell is a Professor Emeritus of Library and Information Scien
 ce in the Faculty of Information and Media Studies\, at the University of 
 Western Ontario in London\, Ontario. He holds a PhD in English Literature 
 from Queen’s University and a Master of Information Studies from the Uni
 versity of Toronto. A violinist for over 50 years\, he has played in numer
 ous community orchestras\, and has also conducted music sessions in variou
 s dementia settings in Toronto and London.\n​\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7224bbb46787079ead9120
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
