DESCRIPTION:This class is for beginners who are curious about buying an An
 droid phone or tablet\, or who have acquired one and want to install apps.
  Android phones include those manufactured by Samsung\, Google\, Motorola\
 , and OnePlus.\nIn this beginner's class\, you will learn about:\n- what a
 pps are\, and the benefits of using them\n- the differences between pre-in
 stalled\, free\, and paid apps\n- how to access and use the Google Play St
 ore\n- how to evaluate\, download and use apps\nAt the end of the class\, 
 you will have a basic understanding of how to install apps on your Android
  device through the Google Play Store.\nBring your own device: if you have
  an Android device\, feel free to bring it with you and follow along with 
 the exercises.\nPrerequisites:  None\nFormat:  Lecture with hands-on exerc
 ises\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
