SUMMARY:Pitch Perfect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T150000
UID:6a5668b5aa34e23600ef0ddc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've spent 8 weeks building your business story\, getting cl
 ear on your customer\, and figuring out your offer. Now it's time to say i
 t out loud. This session teaches you how to craft a clear\, confident 1-mi
 nute pitch for your business - one that actually lands.\nPlease note:  Reg
 istered participant spaces will be held for 15 minutes after which drop-in
 s will be allowed.\nMeet the Resident:\nVivian Kaye is a serial entreprene
 ur and business mentor who bootstrapped KinkyCurlyYaki to seven figures wi
 thout outside funding. Over 15 years\, she has mentored 300+ entrepreneurs
 \, recently facilitating workshops for FoundHers Innovation Labs and Humbe
 r College's Entrepreneurship Program.\nFeatured in The New York Times\, To
 ronto Star\, and on CityTV's Cityline\, Vivian has partnered with brands i
 ncluding Shopify\, Amazon\, and American Express Canada. Her direct\, prac
 tical approach helps early-stage Black entrepreneurs navigate the realitie
 s of building sustainable businesses without traditional support systems.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
