DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T193000
UID:6a466fac9ec85be793f1179c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Emancipation Month with a musical and interactive p
 resentation!\nLed by Frances Greenidge\,\nNature's Enduring Gifts\nis an o
 rganic retelling of the impact of the American folksong\,\nFollow the Drin
 king Gourd\n\, used by fugitive slaves in the mid-1800s to remember and fo
 llow the clues in nature as they journeyed toward freedom in Canada along 
 the Underground Railroad.\nSpace is limited\; online registration is encou
 raged\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
