BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fact or Fiction: Identifying and Combatting Misinformation and Di
 sinformation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T153000
UID:6a50fe23c7e02e3d00681ff2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to separate fact from fiction in a world filled 
 with misinformation and disinformation? Join us for an interactive and ent
 ertaining program where we'll dive into the fascinating world of misinform
 ation\, exploring its origins\, impact\, and how to combat it effectively.
 \nThis program is perfect for curious minds who want to arm themselves wit
 h the skills needed to navigate the complex landscape of online informatio
 n responsibly and safely.\nRegistration is required via tpl.ca or by calli
 ng 416-396-8943.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre (LC)\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a50fe23c7e02e3d00681ff2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Managing Invasive Plants Around Your Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T183000
UID:6a6231364523092f00320c63@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for a presentation o
 n invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. Learn how to ide
 ntify these species\, understand their impact\, and how to manage them.\nY
 ou’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing n
 ative habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeowners\, and anyone interested
  in urban ecology.\nNo registration required. This is a drop-in program.\n
 This program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, suppor
 ted by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6231364523092f00320c63
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Evening Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T200000
UID:6a60c4c69943bdf31ea0b2cd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the 3rd Tuesday evening of every month to discuss b
 ooks in a friendly and social atmosphere.\nAugust Book Title:\nThe Laundry
 man's Boy\nby\nEdward Y.C. Lee\nSeptember Book Title:\nBreakfast of Champi
 ons\, Or\, Goodbye Blue Monday!\nby\nKurt Vonnegut\nTo get a copy of the b
 ook\, please visit the 1st floor desk at Albert Campbell Library. New memb
 ers are always welcome.\nDrop-in or register for a reminder at 416-396-889
 0 or speak to staff at the desk.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a60c4c69943bdf31ea0b2cd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
