BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Small Business Health & Safety Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T190000
UID:6a551594dee4ff5300c931d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As a small business owner\, you have legal obligations when it
  comes to the health and safety of your\nworkplace. But it's not just abou
 t the law. A sound workplace health and safety program will also ensure\nt
 he growth of your business.\n\nDon’t know how to start? This presentatio
 n will guide you through the journey.\n\nWhat you will learn:\n• Who are
  Workplace Safety & Prevention Services (WSPS)?\n• What is the occupatio
 nal health and safety system in Ontario?\n• What is the Occupation Healt
 h & Safety Act (OHSA)?\n• What are responsibilities of the employer\, th
 e supervisor\, and the worker in health & safety?\n• How can I use WSPS 
 Small Business Centre?\n• What other free resources does WSPS provide?\n
 • What is WSIB’s Health & Safety Excellence program (HSEp)?\n\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answ
 erline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a551594dee4ff5300c931d4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: Healing\, Releasing\, and Moving Forward
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T200000
UID:6a4eb7451006a63d00210bc5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Life can bring heavy burdens—grief\, loss\, or the silent ex
 haustion of caring for others. When we experience major heartbreaks\, our 
 emotional energy can feel stuck or overwhelming. You do not have to carry 
 this weight alone. This compassionate workshop offers a safe\, gentle\, a
 nd confidential space for women to honor their feelings\, release emotiona
 l pain\, and find a sense of peace.\nWhat We Will Explore:\nThe Weight of 
 Grief: How our bodies and minds hold onto unexpressed pain and stress.\nGe
 ntle Releasing: Simple\, compassionate mindfulness and breathing exercises
  to practice "letting go.\nShared Strength: Connecting with other women in
  a supportive\, non-judgmental circle.\nThis program is offered through th
 e library settlement partnership for newcomers as such the program will b
 e offered in English and Mandarin. To register please contact Wen Chen at
  647-388-3762 or wchen@ccscan.ca
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Multipurpose Room\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4eb7451006a63d00210bc5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
