BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T153000
UID:69a8a0598b29ea2800d416ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Runnymede branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variet
 y of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the n
 atural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize differe
 nt species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n
 Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nDrop-in. Pro
 gram will be capped at the first 25 participants.\nThe tour will start and
  end at the Runnymede branch and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urb
 an Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route.
  Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. glove
 s/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program ta
 kes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, regist
 rants will be notified of an alternative date.\nThis program is part of TP
 L's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto 
 Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Runnymede
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a8a0598b29ea2800d416ff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Festival Select: Red Eye (Wes Craven\, 2005)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T203000
UID:6a4ea28c4523092f002e9a36@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the Society and Recreation department of the North York C
 entral Library for monthly screenings of fiction and non-fiction films tha
 t push the boundaries of the medium. This month we are showing Wes Craven'
 s\nRed Eye\n(2005).\nSynopsis (Criterion Pictures): Lisa Reisert (Rachel 
 McAdams) hates to fly\, but the terror that awaits her on the night flight
  to Miami has nothing to do with a fear of flying. Moments after takeoff\,
  Lisa's charming seat-mate\, Jackson (Cillian Murphy)\, menacingly reveals
  the real reason he's on board: He is an operative in a plot to kill a ric
 h and powerful businessman... and Lisa is the key to its success. If she r
 efuses to cooperate\, her own father will be killed by an assassin awaitin
 g a call from Jackson. Trapped within the confines of a jet at 30\,000 fee
 t\, Lisa has nowhere to run and no way to summon help without endangering 
 her father\, her fellow passengers and her own life. As the miles tick by\
 , Lisa knows she is running out of time as she desperately looks for a way
  to thwart her ruthless captor and stop a terrible murder.\nNo registratio
 n required.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4ea28c4523092f002e9a36
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T150000
UID:698bcbf87d180d0d4833345c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing\n
 Rouge\nby Mona Awad.\nWhen Belle returns to La Jolla for her beauty-obsess
 ed mother’s funeral\, she is lured into a surreal\, cult-like world cent
 ered around a mysterious spa and its glowing red jellyfish. This descent i
 nto "Sephora Horror" blends grief with gory mayhem to expose the suffocati
 ng toxicity of the beauty industry. Ultimately\, it is a ferocious fairy t
 ale about the dangerous obsession with eternal youth.\nPick up a physical 
 copy at the branch before the meeting\, or find copies through our website
  in various formats. Registration is required and begins Aug. 27\, 2026.\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bcbf87d180d0d4833345c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
