BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dystopia Nonfiction Book Club: A Good War
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T153000
UID:6a5f7868f4e5db3d00c32e07@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us each month to discuss issues in politics and society\,
  and explore how powerful forces are exploiting our world and dystopian im
 aginings are becoming present-day realities.\nOctober’s book is\nA Good 
 War: Mobilizing Canada for the Climate Emergency\nby public policy advisor
  Seth Klein. Copies of the book are available in print\, eBook & eAudiob
 ook format. Book club attendees are encouraged to read the book in advan
 ce of the meeting.\n"In A Good War\, Seth Klein explores how we can align 
 our politics and economy with what the science says we must do to address 
 the climate crisis. But Klein brings an original and uniquely hopeful take
  to this challenge. The book is structured around lessons from the Second 
 World War – the last time Canada faced an existential threat. Others hav
 e said we need a “wartime approach” to climate change\, but this is th
 e first book to delve into what that could actually look like. Canada’s 
 wartime experience\, Klein contends\, provides an inspirational reminder t
 hat\nwe have done this before\n. We have mobilized in common cause across 
 class\, race and gender\, and entirely retooled our economy in the space o
 f a few short years."\nDrop in. No registration required.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Lower Level\, Room B1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5f7868f4e5db3d00c32e07
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
