DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T180000
UID:6a5e83f3f213992f00c5b40c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:By using donated fabrics\, participants will learn how to use 
 shape and textiles to create a textile painting. This workshop will help y
 oung artists gain a better understanding of the elements and principles of
  art and design by understanding texture\, colour\, and dimension by worki
 ng with materials that can be reused. Textiles are easily collected as an 
 item that might be discarded\, initiating the conversation of art making w
 ith upcycled materials. This workshop can be modified for different age gr
 oups by adjusting the adhesive methods from glue to sewing.\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
