BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dufferin/St. Clair Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T200000
UID:6958356a1e64afd01e520492@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us the first Tuesday of each month to discuss books in a 
 fun and friendly atmosphere.\nCopies are available for pickup at the Duffe
 rin/St. Clair branch each month\, or place your own hold to have a copy se
 nt to your closest branch.\nAugust:\nThe Covenant of Water\nby Abraham Ve
 rghese\nSeptember:\nPurity\nby Jonathan Frazen\nOctober:\nThe Edible Woman
 \nby Margaret Atwood\nNovember:\nSlammerkin\nby Emma Donoghue\nDecember:\
 nWhat We Can Know\nby Ian McEwan
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Earlscourt Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6958356a1e64afd01e520492
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
