BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start & Grow Your Business with TSBEC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T183000
UID:6a087391278f7c2f008d8a96@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Information session on how to start\, plan\, finance and grow 
 your very own small business.\nOwning a business is a dream for many peopl
 e. Every new business starts with an idea. This interactive presentation w
 ill give an overview of how to make it happen and the opportunity to ask q
 uestions related to your business. An advisor from TSBEC (Toronto Small B
 usiness Enterprise Centre\, formerly Enterprise Toronto) will present an 
 overview of information related to the business planning process\, evaluat
 ing a business idea\, financing\, marketing planning\, business structures
 \, regulatory requirements\, and more.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a087391278f7c2f008d8a96
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T130000
UID:6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2755@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Tuesdays\, join us for crafts
  (11am-1pm) a walk (11:15am-1pm) and chair yoga (11:30am-12:30pm).\nSnacks
  and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will
  be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGer
 stein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Varies by program
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2755
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
