BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Fatyma Khan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260830T235959
UID:6a676290c7e02e3d006bed48@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of August\, works by artist Fatyma Khan a
 re on display at North York Central Library branch.\nFatyma Khan is an awa
 rd-winning abstract art photographer based in Toronto.\nFatyma Khan's work
  delves into the intricate relationship between individuals and their envi
 ronments\, emphasizing textural composition and the evocative study of lig
 ht. Fatyma’s photography is marked by a contemplative approach\, capturi
 ng the emotional and psychological landscapes shaped by spatial context. H
 er images often reflect the subtle tension between inner experience and ou
 tward reality\, offering viewers a space to engage with the layered comple
 xities of perception\, presence\, and place.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL'
 s\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for 
 local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city. These ex
 hibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its n
 eighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during North York Central Librar
 y open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd floor Gallery space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a676290c7e02e3d006bed48
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
