BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T150000
UID:698bcb20cbf1533ca536cabd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing\n
 All This and More\nby Peng Shepherd.\nDesperate for a second chance\, fort
 y-five-year-old Marsh joins\nAll This and More\n\, a global sensation usin
 g quantum technology to let contestants revise their histories. But as she
  crafts a seemingly perfect existence\, the glossy promise of the show beg
 ins to fracture\, revealing a reality that may be too good to be true. Thi
 s gripping story puts the reader in the driver’s seat\, challenging you 
 to navigate the fine line between fixing the past and losing oneself entir
 ely.\nPick up a physical copy at the branch before the meeting\, or find c
 opies through our website in various formats. Registration is required and
  begins Jul. 23\, 2026.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bcb20cbf1533ca536cabd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
