BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: The Shining
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T150000
UID:697103752c65973d001911c2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This year's Halloween film!\nJack Torrance (Jack Nicholson) be
 comes winter caretaker at the isolated Overlook Hotel in Colorado\, hoping
  to cure his writer's block. He settles in along with his wife\, Wendy (Sh
 elley Duvall)\, and his son\, Danny (Danny Lloyd)\, who is plagued by psyc
 hic premonitions. As Jack's writing goes nowhere and Danny's visions becom
 e more disturbing\, Jack discovers the hotel's dark secrets and begins to 
 unravel into a homicidal maniac hell-bent on terrorizing his family.\nRate
 d R\n2 Hour 23 Minutes
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, FCCR (First-Floor Auditorium)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697103752c65973d001911c2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Revitalizing Biodiversity in a Toronto Ravine on Public and Privat
 e Land – The Nordheimer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T190000
UID:6a557a85e9de6536001b836d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this presentation\, environmental researcher Susan Aaron wi
 ll explore the following questions: What is a ravine--historically and tod
 ay--as a base for natural revitalization and water retention and human and
  wildlife use? How do ravines reinvent what a city is\, as having a natura
 l base rather than a concrete one? And how might ravines inform us of the 
 linkages across public and private land\, informing both biodiversity and
  sustainability?
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a557a85e9de6536001b836d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
