SUMMARY:Craft Club: Movie Afternoons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T160000
UID:69b057bfb48451fc3c07e9f8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Malvern Library's Craft Club runs twice a month on Tuesdays. 
 Basic supplies provided for learners.\nFirst session\n:\nJoin us in the Di
 gital Innovation Hub to make a crafting-related goodie to take home.\nRegi
 stration required.\nRegister in-person while participating in the previous
  month's session two. Any leftover spots are available to reserve online a
 fter the program ends.\nSecond session:\nDo you knit\, crochet\, hand-sew\
 , cross-stitch\, or embroider? Or are you looking to learn? Join us to st
 itch\, chat\, and have some fun while watching a cozy film.\nDrop-in.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
 ions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for even
 t and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how 
 the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff a
 t\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b057bfb48451fc3c07e9f8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Magical World of Intellectual Property
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T191500
UID:6a5fe5ee3896acb13e3fb0f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This unique​ information seminar informs people with start
 ups\, influencers\, artists\, entertainers and inventors about their inte
 llectual property rights. The presentation shares knowledge about the vari
 ous forms of IP assets– copyright\, trademark\, patents\, trade secrets\
 , contracts– with real world examples with multiple industries. IP plann
 ing and protection strategies will be explained in a fun and interesting p
 rogram by including magical effects during the presentation.\nRegistrati
 on is encouraged\, and we welcome drop in customers until capacity is reac
 hed.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5fe5ee3896acb13e3fb0f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
