BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Historical Fiction Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T200000
UID:69ea4dfc213814b1b524d6e1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in historical people and events?\nJoin our 
 book club where we will read a wide range of historical fiction titles.\nJ
 uly 2:\nA Long Petal of the Sea\nby Isabel Allende\nPlease reserve your ow
 n copy or ask staff for help.\nAug 6:\nThe Nickel Boys\nby Colson Whitehea
 d\nCopies of the book will be available on July 2.\nSept 3:\nThe Night Wat
 chman\nby Louise Erdrich\nPlease reserve your own copy or ask staff for he
 lp.\nOct 1:\nWe Do Not Part\nby Han Kang\nPlease reserve your own copy or 
 ask staff for help.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, In the basement program room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ea4dfc213814b1b524d6e1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creating Suspense in Crime and Mystery Fiction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T200000
UID:69ecbe3bdefec6489cc01ea1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Award-winning crime writer Howard Shrier (\nMontreal Noir\n\;\
 nBuffalo Jump\n) shares techniques for building suspense in stories of cri
 me and mystery. With a short reading of a suspenseful passage from his new
  novel and by drawing on his experience as an author and creative writing 
 teacher\, Howard will show you how to create an outline that takes your ch
 aracters on the most challenging journey possible.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ecbe3bdefec6489cc01ea1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding a Job with ACCES Employment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T193000
UID:69ebdb675c04bc0fc0636d6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interview Preparation & Personal Branding\nThis workshop prepa
 res participants for interviews with a focus on answering behavioral quest
 ions\, articulating their strengths\, and building a strong personal brand
 . Practical tips and examples will be shared\, along with time for Q&A.\nP
 articipants are encouraged (but not required) to bring a copy of their res
 ume (digital or printed) for feedback.\nDrop-In. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room\, Basement Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ebdb675c04bc0fc0636d6d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Microsoft Access 1: An Introduction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T143000
UID:6a468c3ddd4fa0c68b5e8507@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Access is a tool to turn large datasets into a datab
 ase. We will work with some basic concepts to help get started and explore
  the beginner level requirements for our data to work properly.\nConcepts 
 include:\nCreating a table\nThe Primary Key\nNaming practices\nImporting f
 rom Excel\nPlease have taken at least Excel Basics 2 before attending.
LOCATION:Maryvale\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a468c3ddd4fa0c68b5e8507
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Northern District Book Club—Afternoons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T150000
UID:6a5f86b17b79214226aa13af@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a friendly\, spirited discussion of a different bo
 ok on the second Wednesday of each month. We read an eclectic mix of mostl
 y contemporary fiction.\nThere is also an evening session to discuss the s
 ame book on the third Wednesday of each month at 7:00 p.m.  You are welc
 ome at either or both!\nNote:\nno August meeting\nSeptember 9\, 2026:\nOrb
 ital\nby Samantha Harvey\nOctober 14\, 2026:\nMaybe You Should Talk to Som
 eone\nby Lori Gottlieb\nNovember 11\, 2026:\nStone Yard Devotional\nby Cha
 rlotte Wood\nDecember 9\, 2026:\nPerfection\nby Vincenzo Latronico
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5f86b17b79214226aa13af
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LinkedIn 101 with ACCES Employment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T150000
UID:6a4969be0e851028002f43da@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in this interactive workshop to learn how to utilize L
 inkedIn for your job search journey. You will learn strategies for targeti
 ng your LinkedIn profile\, forming connections\, keeping your account acti
 ve\, and reaching out to employers. Please bring your own personal device 
 to follow along.\nRegistration is encouraged on TPL website.\nDrop-ins wel
 come until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4969be0e851028002f43da
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Data Science Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T193000
UID:6a10653dc7d3cd58005ae1d7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about Data Science? Let's take a free o
 nline course together in a welcoming space!\nTogether we will work through
  Cisco Networking Academy's Introduction to Data Science course over six w
 eeks\, where we'll be introduced to basic concepts\, including:\nIntroduct
 ory analytics\nData collection\nData storage\nAI and machine learning\nPar
 ticipants will learn together in a peer-supported environment through a le
 arning circle\, a lightly facilitated study group guided by library staff.
 \nLearners who successfully complete the course will earn a digital badge 
 and certificate of completion.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 
 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
